# ExtensionDataService

Injectable Angular service that wraps the Packages Consumer REST API.

## Location
`src/app/features/extensions/services/extension-data.service.ts`

## Injection
```typescript
private readonly extensionData = inject(ExtensionDataService);
```

## Methods

### `getPackage(applicationId: string, packageId: string): Observable<Package>`
Fetches detailed metadata for a single package.

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}`

**Example:**
```typescript
extensionData.getPackage('ead9f857-5111-4759-a1f9-c75361e0a347', 'cyrena.tavily')
  .subscribe(pkg => console.log(pkg.title, pkg.versions));
```

### `getPackages(applicationId: string, os?: string, arch?: string): Observable<Package[]>`
Lists all packages for an application, optionally filtered by OS and architecture.

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages?os={os}&arch={arch}`

### `getIconUrl(applicationId: string, packageId: string): string`
Returns the URL for the package icon image.

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}/icon`

**Example:**
```typescript
const iconUrl = extensionData.getIconUrl(appId, packageId);
// Returns: "/api/applications/{appId}/packages/{packageId}/icon"
```

### `getDownloadUrl(applicationId: string, packageId: string, version?: string): string`
Returns the download URL for a package. If no version is specified, downloads the latest.

**Endpoint:** `GET /api/applications/{applicationId}/packages/{packageId}/download?version={version}`

## Package Model

See `src/app/features/extensions/models/extensionmodel.model.ts`:

```typescript
interface Package {
  id: string;
  packageId: string;
  title: string | null;
  description: string | null;
  supportedOperatingSystems: string[];
  supportedArchitectures: string[];
  hasIcon: boolean;
  latestVersion: string | null;
  versions: PackageVersion[];
}

interface PackageVersion {
  version: string;
  sizeBytes: number;
  contentHash: string | null;
  createdAt: string;
  releaseNotes: string | null;
}
```

## Base URL
The service uses relative URLs (`/api/...`) because the Packages API runs on the same origin as this Angular application.

## Error Handling
Consumers should handle:
- `404 Not Found` — package does not exist
- `500 Server Error` — retry with exponential backoff
